 "upload": {
  "title": "WMO: Sea Level Hit a Record as El Niño Builds #shorts",
  "description": "The World Meteorological Organization's State of the Climate update, released as COP31 opened in Antalya, says global sea level hit a record high in 2026 and ocean heat set a record in 2025. January–September 2026 averaged about 1.47°C above pre-industrial levels, and WMO says the current El Niño could reach record strength by December.\n\nSources: WMO State of the Climate Update for COP31, reported by UN News, The Irish Times and AFP via Phys.org (based on search-result excerpts). Warm areas on the map are illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #wmo #elnino #cop31",
